    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test class, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nTwo small, cohesive edits so a created/fetched owner returns `displayName` as `LastName, FirstName`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field (no hand-written DTO to touch).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` on the existing `toOwnerDto(Owner)` method computing the value inline from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nBecause both `getOwner` and `addOwner` in the controller already route through `toOwnerDto`, the format is applied on create and on read with no controller or service changes.\n\n## Structural-impact notes\n- Touched 2 files; changed exactly one function (`toOwnerDto`, CC=1) by one annotation line \u2014 no method or class grew in body complexity.\n- Reused the existing single mapping seam rather than adding logic to the controller, service, or `Owner` entity (all of which carry much higher `WMC_other`).",
